   "final_rule_text": "Manufacturers shall report every thermal incident involving overheating, fire, or thermal runaway to the relevant regulator within 5 business days of becoming aware of it, including incidents initially reported by customers or installers. A death, serious injury, evacuation, or spread of fire beyond the battery shall be reported within 24 hours. Manufacturers shall notify affected customers within 5 business days when an incident presents a credible safety risk to their unit or requires inspection, repair, or use precautions. Reports shall include available details and be updated as investigations progress; an incomplete initial report does not excuse timely reporting."
