   "comparison": "weakened by: over_limit_consequence, transition",
   "final_rule_text": "Each model shall undergo a sustained-heat test at 55 °C using a regulator-approved protocol and representative production units before market entry and after a material design change. Manufacturers shall provide complete per-model results, protocol, and sample size to the relevant regulator and to customers considering or owning that model. A failure rate above 5% shall trigger a regulator-reviewed corrective-action plan and follow-up testing; it shall not by itself bar sale. The regulator may require additional safeguards or restrict sales if evidence shows an unresolved, material safety risk."
